{{!
    @template local_ai_course_assistant/analytics_tab_overall

    Overall Usage tab of the analytics dashboard. Replaces the innerHTML string
    that amd/src/analytics_dashboard.js used to build for this pane
    (CONTRIB-10574 #278). The canvases are deliberately empty: Chart.js draws
    into them once the rendered nodes are in the document.

    The three chart headings are still literal English, exactly as they were in
    the JavaScript this replaces. Translating them needs new analytics_js keys
    and is tracked separately under the i18n issue, not here.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * cards - array of stat tiles, each with a value and a label

    Example context (json):
    {
        "cards": [
            {"value": "128", "label": "Total students"},
            {"value": "41", "label": "Active AI users"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="sola-stat-cards">
    {{#cards}}
        <div class="sola-stat-card">
            <div class="sola-stat-value">{{value}}</div>
            <div class="sola-stat-label">{{label}}</div>
        </div>
    {{/cards}}
</div>
<div class="row mt-4">
    <div class="col-md-12 mb-4">
        <h5>Daily Usage Trend</h5>
        <canvas id="sola-chart-daily" height="80"></canvas>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
        <h5>Hour of Day</h5>
        <canvas id="sola-chart-hourly" height="120"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
        <h5>Day of Week</h5>
        <canvas id="sola-chart-dow" height="120"></canvas>
    </div>
</div>
